"Accusers affirm a charge with 'I, [name], have said it is so.'"
"An accused may kneel and ask witnesses to unsay a claim; they confer a pace back, unheard."
"If the first witness refuses, the accused may request honesty verification."
"If a second witness disagrees with the first, more process is required."
"Mercy formula: 'The strong may pull mercy from their pockets without noticing a loss.'"
"The plea 'Is your belly stone, wood, or flesh?' is answered 'Flesh' by one capable of mercy."
